From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Fri Jul  2 05:51:41 2004
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Fri, 02 Jul 2004 06:51:41 +0100
Subject: Re: .First.lib problem
In-Reply-To: <1088728437.3156.20.camel@zwang.stat.smu.edu>
References: <1088728437.3156.20.camel@zwang.stat.smu.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0407020641240.12888-100000@gannet.stats>

You called .First.lib with no arguments and no default arguments.  It 
works if you give it arguments -- that you do not get an error message 
with library(MASS) commented out does not mean it `there is no such 
error', for there is, just no message.

I have no idea why your library section does not work, but any error in 
its .First.lib will abort the process before the last line.  And it does 
not need that dyn.open line as S.dll is automatically loaded.

