Thanks to all. My problem was solved based on Prof. Ripley's
instruction. I think it was because of misunderstanding of function
"library". I was curious about my .First.lib function since I did not
see how the arguments "library" and "section" were used in .First.lib (I
should read the document more carefully), so the mistake is certainly
silly. So I firstly run 

>.First.lib(library, section)

To let the library load my .First.lib, I added it to my function
GWS.funcs, something like below, and rerun the following script:

createChapter(paste(getenv("SHOME"),"\\library\\GWS",sep=""))
library(GWS,lib.loc="C:\\Program
Files\\Insightful\\splus6\\library\\GWS")
mkdir(paste(getenv("SHOME"),"\\library\\GWS\\.Prefs",sep=""))
mkdir(paste(getenv("SHOME"),"\\library\\GWS\\_Data\\_Help",sep=""))
library(GWS,first=T)
database.name(where=9)
GWS.funcs<-c("create.menu.gws","remove.menu.gws",".First.lib",".Last.lib")
database.status(where=9, meta=0)<- "modified"
for(i in 1:length(GWS.funcs)){
assign(GWS.funcs[i], get(GWS.funcs[i]),where=9)
}

Whether because of this change or not, maybe not necessarily, now it
works!

