Subject: summing over parts of a data.frame
Message-ID: <40E94116.1020507@uni-jena.de>

Dear all,

I have a (n x k ) dataframe (with n rows and k columns), and I would 
like to sum over every row (including only the 4th to kth column), such 
that I´d have a variable containing the row sum for a subset of the 
dataframe.

So far, I´ve been trying something like:

rowsum_0
for (i in 3:ncol(data)){
for (k in 1:nrow(data)){
   rowsum[k]_data[k,i]+data[k+1,i]}
}

but it doesn´t give me the result I would like. Can anyone help?

Cheers & thanks very much in advance,
Chris

From dimitrios.rizopoulos at student.kuleuven.ac.be  Mon Jul  5 12:00:33 2004
From: dimitrios.rizopoulos at student.kuleuven.ac.be (Dimitris Rizopoulos)
Date: Mon, 05 Jul 2004 14:00:33 +0200
Subject: Re: summing over parts of a data.frame
References: <40E94116.1020507@uni-jena.de>
Message-ID: <002b01c46287$ae460d30$ad133a86@www.domain>

Hi Chris,

If your data.frame contains numeric variables you can easily transform
it to matrix, e.g., using "data.matrix()" and then use something like,

apply(dat, 1, function(x, k) sum(x[4:k]), k=ncol(x))

I hope this helps.

Best,
Dimitris

