If I understand correctly your concern is that SAS Marginal means are 
different from the means calculated from your data.  If so I would recomend 
you to review what actually are the marginal means (model dependent means).  
Also you mention that you are trying to make multiple paired t-tests but if 
you have more than 2 measures then your comparisons will be biased (that is 
why you are suing repeated measures analysis in the first place isn't?).  
Check ?lme from the nlme4 library at S-Plus to do this.  Once you build a 
proper model you can use custom contrasts (check ?contrasts) to compare lung 
function @ condition 1 vs. 2, 3 and 4.

