I suspect that try() can be used to suit your needs.

> echk1 <- c(9, 16, 25) 

> sqrt(echk1) 

[1] 3 4 5

> try(sqrt(echk1)) 

[1] 3 4 5

> is(try(sqrt(echk1)), "Error")

[1] F

> echk2 <- c(9, "h", 25) 

> sqrt(echk2) 

Problem in x^0.5: Non-numeric first operand

Evaluation frames saved in object "last.dump", use debugger()
to examine them

> x <- try(sqrt(echk2))

> x

[1] "Problem in x^0.5: Non-numeric first operand"

attr(, "class"):

[1] "Error"

> is(x, "Error")

[1] T

> 

> 

(Note that this works more cleanly in S-plus 6.2 than in S-plus
6.1.  Also note that try() does not work properly when nested, in
both S-plus 6.2 and S-plus 6.1)

-- Tony Plate

