Subject: Re: Problem in solve.qr(a): Apparently singular matrix
Message-ID: <3F446F20E557604A9A5B9D49E3F76FDA9E9E1D@exnsw2-syd.nexus.csiro.au>

Hi Zhu,

You might be able to get around this by changing the tolerance in the QR
decomposition. qr() takes a tolerance argument but you cannot control it
from solve. If you modify the solve.default function like this:

solve.default <- function(a, b, tol = 1e-007)
{
        if(!(missing(b) || is.numeric(b) || mode(b) == "complex"))
                stop("b must be numeric or complex")
        if(!is.list(a))
                a <- qr(a, tol = tol)
        if(missing(b))
                solve.qr(a)
        else solve.qr(a, b)
}

you can then specify the tolerance.

Cheers,
Tim Keighley

