Hi -

I think what you are looking for is "output buffering" that collects 
output and displays it only if a certain amount of output is in the 
buffer.
Go to "Options" - "General Settings" - "Output Buffering" and uncheck 
"Buffer Output" (S-Plus 6.1). I am not sure though if that option already 
existed in S-Plus 2000.
The output - even if buffered - does not disappear if the S-Plus window is 
not refreshed (my inference based on my observations using S-Plus 6.1 on 
Windows XP). Try not to work in other windows that overlap your S-Plus 
window or not to move them across the S-Plus window.

        Andreas Krause

