It was as simple as that:

Before trying my script I had locally tweaked the general
settings [from the GUI] to return timeDate output in dd/MM/yy.

So my call produced

> (as.character(timeSeq("01/01/03","03/01/03",by="days")))

[1] "01/01/03"
"02/01/03" "03/01/03"

Surprisingly, running the logical test (==”01/01/03”) kept
failing and I could not see my error!

Specifying the output format from within the function produces
the required result:

> (as.character(timeSeq("01/01/03","03/01/03",by="days",format="%02d/%02m/%02y")))=="01/01/03"

[1] T F F

 

Given the lessons from this I am wondering whether tweaking
the general settings from the GUI is of any practical use (?)

